Source: voxtype
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
# Nothing is compiled; dpkg-shlibdeps needs the libraries the prebuilt binaries link to
# installed in the build chroot to work out ${shlibs:Depends}.
 libasound2t64,
 libvulkan1,
 libgtk-4-1,
 libgtk4-layer-shell0,
 libcairo2,
 libglib2.0-0t64
Standards-Version: 4.7.4
Homepage: https://voxtype.io
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: voxtype
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends},
 curl
Recommends: pipewire-alsa, wtype, wl-clipboard
Suggests: libnotify-bin
Description: push-to-talk voice-to-text for Wayland
 Voxtype records while a key is held (or between two presses), transcribes
 the speech on this machine with a Whisper or Parakeet model, and types the
 text into the focused window. No audio leaves the machine.
 .
 This package holds Voxtype's own release builds: the CPU builds (AVX2,
 AVX-512 and baseline), the Vulkan build for GPUs from NVIDIA, AMD and
 Intel, the CPU builds of the ONNX (Parakeet) engine, and the on-screen
 display. /usr/bin/voxtype picks the build: the Vulkan one when VOXTYPE_GPU=1,
 otherwise the best CPU build. Voxtype's ONNX GPU builds (CUDA and MIGraphX)
 are left out: they need NVIDIA's CUDA or AMD's ROCm runtime.
